    <section class="hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="kicker">Property in Peru, with someone on the ground</p>
        <h1>An 8×20 meter lot, or about 100 hectares of forest.</h1>
        <p class="lede">I help people in other countries buy property in Peru. A small lot, in the right town, can start around a few thousand dollars. A house, an apartment, or a large piece of forest or farmland is the same careful work at another scale. You can hold land and build later. You can sell later. Neither is a promise that the price will rise.</p>
        <div class="range">
          <div>
            <strong>8×20 m</strong>
            <p>A small urban or town lot. In some places the asking price is a few thousand dollars. In Lima’s central districts it is not.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="range-line" role="presentation"></div>
          <div>
            <strong>About 100 hectares</strong>
            <p>Forest or agricultural land. Title, access, water, and the border zone matter more here, not less.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="btn" href="start.html">Start with what you want</a>
          <a class="btn secondary" href="scout.html">How a scouting visit works</a>
        </div>
