    <section class="section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>Three ways people arrive</h2>
        <div class="grid-3">
          <article class="card coast">
            <h3>You want to live there</h3>
            <p>Retirement, a long stay, or a base for part of the year. The first job is the climate, the hospital, and whether you can stand the daily noise. The listing comes after that.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card sand">
            <h3>You want to hold, and build later</h3>
            <p>Land can sit while you decide. Building, a water tank, a roof, and a road are a second project. I will not pretend the empty lot is the whole cost.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card forest">
            <h3>You care about the price</h3>
            <p>I have bought and sold for a profit by knowing local price ranges. That is experience, not a forecast. Resale is possible. It is not guaranteed. Values can fall.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="wrap measure">
        <h2>Who is writing this</h2>
        <p>I was born in the United States. I later became a naturalized Peruvian citizen. I bought property here before that change, and again after it. I have lived in various parts of Peru. I know the climates, the food, and the ordinary pace of the place, not only the airport road.</p>
        <p>I am not your lawyer, your notary, or your tax advisor. I do not present myself as a registered <span lang="es">agente inmobiliario</span>. I guide the process and I do the on-the-ground scouting. For the legal transaction I partner with an independent <span lang="es">abogado</span> and an independent <span lang="es">notario</span>.</p>
        <p>I center the work on places I know well enough to walk. I cannot honestly scout every region of Peru in person. When another region is the right fit, a trusted local contact does the visit, and I stay on the file so the standard does not drop.</p>
        <p><a href="about.html">What I do, and what I will not do</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>

